{"assets":["/statement-assets/6dd1fe0159e776a5dcc5ed23002c23f89347aea0cc6ca2599921d8bc700b7b0c.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"350","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Wrong Floyd"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Valera conducts experiments with algorithms that search for shortest paths. He has recently studied the Floyd's algorithm, so it's time to work with it."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Valera's already written the code that counts the shortest distance between any pair of vertexes in a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-directed connected graph"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" from "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertexes and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" edges, containing no loops and multiple edges. Besides, Valera's decided to mark part of the vertexes. He's marked exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertexes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., ak"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Valera's code is given below."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nans[i][j] // the shortest distance for a pair of vertexes i, j\na[i]  // vertexes, marked by Valera\n\nfor(i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n    for(j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n        if (i == j)\n            ans[i][j] = 0;\n        else\n            ans[i][j] = INF;  //INF is a very large number \n    }\n}    \n\nfor(i = 1; i <= m; i++) {\n    read a pair of vertexes u, v that have a non-directed edge between them;\n    ans[u][v] = 1;\n    ans[v][u] = 1;\n}\n\nfor (i = 1; i <= k; i++) {\n    v = a[i];\n    for(j = 1; j <= n; j++)\n        for(r = 1; r <= n; r++)\n            ans[j][r] = min(ans[j][r], ans[j][v] + ans[v][r]);\n}\n"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Valera has seen that his code is wrong. Help the boy. Given the set of marked vertexes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ..., ak"},{"kind":"text","text":", find such "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"non-directed connected graph"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" vertexes and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" edges, for which Valera's code counts the wrong shortest distance for at least one pair of vertexes "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(i, j)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Valera is really keen to get a graph without any loops and multiple edges. If no such graph exists, print -1."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of the input contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n, m, k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3 ≤ n ≤ 300"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2 ≤ k ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":" , "},{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/6dd1fe0159e776a5dcc5ed23002c23f89347aea0cc6ca2599921d8bc700b7b0c.png"},"kind":"image"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the number of vertexes, the number of edges and the number of marked vertexes. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of the input contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" space-separated integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1, a2, ... ak"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ ai ≤ n"},{"kind":"text","text":") — the numbers of the marked vertexes. It is guaranteed that all numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" are distinct."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If the graph doesn't exist, print -1 on a single line. Otherwise, print "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines, each containing two integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"u, v"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the description of the edges of the graph Valera's been looking for."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 2 2\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 3\n2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 3 2\n1 2\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"350E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/350/problem/E"}